  "units": "cm",
  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for the images in a convex lens, book pages 259–264, topic 9.4.2, next to চিত্র ৯.২১–৯.২৬. A glass biconvex lens (f = 15 cm) stands in its ring on an optical bench with a printed cm scale, the book's pencil XY on its left and a paper screen on its right. Parallel light from far away gathers at the focus F′ on a screen (the book's নিজে করো) and light from a point at F leaves parallel; the book's three rays from the pencil's tip meet at X′, where a screen catches a sharp, real, inverted image. The student moves the pencil through the book's cases (inside F: virtual, upright, bigger, seen by an eye through the lens; between F and 2F; at 2F; beyond 2F), sees the book's উদাহরণ (object and image change places), a live graph of image distance against object distance and a summary table, then takes a five-question test.",
